            <ArticleTitle>[Peridural administration of drugs in root-compression forms of lumbar osteochondrosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>523-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Following a prolonged and unsuccessful treatment, 50 patients with severe compression-radical forms of lumbar osteochondritis received--under roentgenographic control--a course of epidural injections of drugs (trimecaine, chymotrypsin and lydasa). A considerable improvement was observed in 60% of the patients, which indicates that the method is effective.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
